Fixes: exportToBlob/exportToCanvas/exportToSvg are not exported from ../index or from @excalidraw/utils; they are module-private in packages/excalidraw/scene/export.ts. Use exportScene, exported from ../index (index.tsx line 427): it takes ONE options object, exportScene({ type: "svg" | "canvas" | "png", ...ExportSceneOptions }) (packages/excalidraw/scene/export.ts ~line 1418); read ExportSceneOptions there for the elements, appState, files and embed-scene fields. SEARCH_SIDEBAR_TAB does not exist in @excalidraw/common: the constant is CANVAS_SEARCH_TAB, and the file's vi.mock of @excalidraw/common must spread importOriginal() so real exports stay available. For the undo test: read history.ts and App.tsx; if the test's page-A step creates the element and then undoes, undo correctly removes it — make the test edit an existing page-A element (e.g. move it) before switching, and assert the edit is undone on page A and nothing changes on page B. Do not weaken the page-isolation assertions.

The file's current text is under Inputs, marked "current text"; your edits apply to exactly that text.

## Answer
Return ONLY a JSON object {"path": "packages/excalidraw/tests/pages.test.tsx", "edits": [{"search": "<text copied exactly from the current text>", "replace": "<its replacement>"}]} with no other text. Each search must appear exactly once in the current text; the edits apply in order.
If the file does not exist yet, or the change rewrites most of it, return {"path": "packages/excalidraw/tests/pages.test.tsx", "content": "<the complete file>"} instead.
